            <div xml:id="d492">

                <pb facs="0634" n="522" sameAs="frus:frus1935v03/pg522"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">123J634/354: Telegram</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Secretary of State to the Minister in China</hi>
                        (<hi rendition="#italic">Johnson</hi>)</head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Washington</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1935-06-21T18:00:00-04:00">June 21, 1935—6 p.m.</date></dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>181. Your nomination was confirmed by Senate June 14th and President has
                    appointed you June 18th to be Ambassador Extraordinary and Plenipotentiary of
                    the United States to China. Letter of credence being mailed to you care of
                    Consulate General Nanking on steamer <hi rendition="#italic">President
                        Grant</hi> from Seattle June 22nd. Your status as Minister will continue
                    until day you present credentials Nanking. On that day you will take oath as
                    Ambassador. Salary at $17,500 per annum begins when letter of credence
                    presented. Deficiency appropriation is being requested and it is expected this
                    will be approved by time you <pb facs="0635" n="523" xml:id="pg523"/> are ready
                    to present credentials. If deficiency appropriation delayed for any reason,
                    further instructions will be issued in due time. Your traveling expenses and
                    usual per diem on trip to Nanking should be charged to item for travel in your
                    district as already established in Legation’s regular contingent expense
                    allotment for coming fiscal year.</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Hull</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
